        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Financial Accounting",
        "topic": "Accounting Equation",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2001",
        "question_text": "<p>If assets are $50,000 and liabilities are $20,000, what is the owner's equity?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The accounting equation is: <b>Assets = Liabilities + Owner's Equity</b>.<br>Rearranged: <b>Owner's Equity = Assets - Liabilities</b>.<br>Thus, $50,000 - $20,000 = $30,000.</p>",
